    {
      "id": "claim_b7eafe9d0a054a918dca12a6a97376cc",
      "statement": "The documented replication-package workflow layers LOCAL underneath a shared remote cache (CACHE_HIERARCHY=REDIS,LOCAL or REST_REDIS,LOCAL): HierarchicalCache writes every put through to all layers and backfills entries present in one layer but missing in another on read, so after the run the local directory holds everything the run touched; callers then flush via CacheManager.getDefaultInstance().flush() and ship the directory, and replicators re-run offline with CACHE_HIERARCHY=LOCAL.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L306-L322",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5369d3657c36ec902a63d41c0be4e0d93a75b7a75c86b7e4529badd1aaa448cf:"
